# GitHub issue #15

**Repository:** alexisNorthcoders/snake-colyseus
**URL:** https://github.com/alexisNorthcoders/snake-colyseus/issues/15
**State:** OPEN
**Labels:** ready-for-agent
**Title:** Single-use rooms

## Body
## What to build

Public rooms become single-use. A room locks when a round starts, so matchmaking never puts a player into a room mid-round, and it never unlocks: `ended` is terminal (`reusable: false` for the public room). A `startGame` received after the round ended is ignored. The room is disposed once the last player leaves.

Part of fixing the "invisible snake after Play Again" bug: rounds are never restarted in the same room, so clients never have to reset a previous round's state. The client side (Play Again → fresh lobby) is tracked in alexisNorthcoders/snake-phaser#92.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] Room locks on round start; a new `joinOrCreate` during `playing` or `ended` lands in a different room
- [ ] `ended` is terminal for the public room; `startGame` after `ended` is ignored
- [ ] Room disposes when empty
- [ ] Late-join-mid-round path (joiner sits out) is no longer reachable and is removed
- [ ] Tests cover locking, terminal `ended`, and ignored `startGame`

